// A bare-metal target runs one isolate, its core: a module `static` is one plain C global there, so a second isolate would
// share the first one's. `spawn` is refused there, as `spawn fiber` is (KR-341); a second core is KR-346.
fn void blink(int32 times) { }
fn uint8 main() {
    scope { spawn blink(times: 3); }
    return 0;
}
